    "preview_note": "HD reports Q2 FY26 (quarter ended Aug 2) against its toughest compare and peak spring selling season. The setup: Q1 printed comps of +0.6% (US +0.4%) with adjusted EPS down 3.7% to $3.43, and management reaffirmed FY26 guidance of +2.5-4.5% total sales and flat-to-+4% adjusted EPS. Three factors decide the print. First, comp trajectory: Q2 laps last year's +1.0% total comp with GMS now in the base for the full quarter; FX adds ~50-60bp and tariff-related ticket inflation helps, but housing turnover remains the ceiling on big-ticket demand. Second, margin: GMS dilution and SRS integration drove the 100bp Q1 operating-margin decline; watch whether gross margin holds ~33% and whether SG&A leverage improves on the larger sales base. Third, guidance: with one soft quarter in the books, any trim to the comp or EPS range resets the year. We model revenue of $46.7B (+3.2%), adjusted EPS of $4.64 (down ~1% YoY), and free cash flow of ~$2.7B as seasonal working capital reverses. The reaction hinges on comps and the guide: a hold with comps >= +1.5% is fine; a cut is not.",
